## Flags

[image-20261029-200106.png]

### Example flag response

Below is the payload the CDB UI receives from LD for the context above. Each top-level key is a flag key.

```json
{
  "ALERTS":                { "flagVersion": 2,  "trackEvents": false, "value": false,         "variation": 1, "version": 133 },
  "BENEFITS_HUB":          { "flagVersion": 38, "trackEvents": false, "value": true,          "variation": 0, "version": 133 },
  "CDB_KILL_SWITCH":       { "flagVersion": 2,  "trackEvents": false, "value": false,         "variation": 1, "version": 133 },
  "CLICK_TO_PAY":          { "flagVersion": 31, "trackEvents": false, "value": true,          "variation": 0, "version": 133 },
  "MOBILE_QR_CODE":        { "flagVersion": 65, "trackEvents": false, "value": true,          "variation": 0, "version": 133 },
  "bdc-role":              { "flagVersion": 5,  "trackEvents": false, "value": false,         "variation": 1, "version": 133 },
  "channels_allow_budget": { "flagVersion": 2,  "trackEvents": false, "value": "MBA,MBW,OLB", "variation": 1, "version": 133 },
  "role_allow_budget":     { "flagVersion": 2,  "trackEvents": false, "value": "variation 2", "variation": 1, "version": 133 }
}
```

### Response fields

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `value` | The evaluated flag value the app should use (boolean, string, etc.) |
| `variation` | Index of the variation served (0 = first variation defined on the flag) |
| `flagVersion` | Version of this flag's config; increments each time the flag is changed |
| `version` | Version of the overall LD environment data at evaluation time |
| `trackEvents` | Whether detailed evaluation events are sent back to LD for this flag |

> Note: flags can return non-boolean values. `channels_allow_budget` returns a string list (`"MBA,MBW,OLB"`), so the UI must parse it rather than treat it as on/off.

